# Module-Owned Migrations

When changing DB schema in a module, add migrations **inside the module**, not in root `supabase/migrations`.

## Where to put migrations

- **Path**: `modules/<module-name>/supabase/migrations/`
- **Filename**: `YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_plugin_<slug>.sql` (slug must start with `plugin_`)
- **Uniqueness**: No two modules may use the same migration basename

## Committed vs local (generated from engenty.plugins)

Enabled modules are declared in root **`package.json` → `engenty.plugins`**. Compose pipelines (Supabase, migrations aggregate, UI catalog, runtime discovery) use that map — not every folder under `modules/` on disk.

| Artifact | In git | Created by |
|----------|--------|------------|
| `modules/*/supabase/migrations/*.sql` | ✅ | Module |
| root `package.json` → `engenty.plugins` | ✅ | Product manifest |
| `supabase/config.toml.example` | ✅ module-agnostic base | Repo |
| `supabase/migrations/*.sql` | ❌ gitignored | `engenty setup` |
| `supabase/config.toml` | ❌ gitignored | `engenty setup` |
| `apps/ui/src/plugins/generated-catalog.ts` | ❌ gitignored | `engenty setup` |
| `apps/ui/src/plugins/generated-tailwind-sources.css` | ❌ gitignored | `engenty setup` |

After clone: **`pnpm engenty setup --local`**. When changing the module set or module SQL: **`pnpm engenty setup`** then **`pnpm db:migrate`** (or **`pnpm db:init`** on a fresh DB).

## Do / Don't

```bash
# ✅ Add migration in the module (plugin_ prefix required)
# modules/team/supabase/migrations/20260227120000_plugin_team_avatar.sql

# ❌ Do not commit *_plugin_*.sql in supabase/migrations (gitignored)
# ❌ Do not commit supabase/config.toml or generated UI plugin artifacts
```

## Commands

- **First-run / module set changed**: `pnpm engenty setup --local` (first clone) or `pnpm engenty setup`
- **Add module to manifest**: `pnpm engenty plugins enable <slug>`
- **Compose Supabase only**: `engenty db sync`
- **Apply or push**: `pnpm db:migrate` or `pnpm db:init` on a fresh DB

Full details: [plugins.md](../../../docs/content/dev/plugins.md).
